---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<SiteLayout
  page="privacy"
  title="Privacy Policy — Stimmyz"
  description="Draft privacy policy for Stimmyz, the Android soundboard app. Learn how the app accesses, stores, and handles user-created audio and artwork."
  themeColor="#fbfaf7"
  noIndex={true}
>
  <main id="main">
    <div class="container policy-top">
      <div class="eyebrow">YOUR PRIVACY MATTERS</div>
      <h1>
        Privacy Policy<span class="ink-accent">.</span>
      </h1>
      <p>
        How Stimmyz handles recordings, imported sounds, artwork, and your
        choices.
      </p>
      <div class="policy-timestamp">
        Draft prepared: October 25, 2026 · Applies to the Stimmyz Android app
        and this website
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="container policy-content">
      <aside class="policy-toc">
        <strong>ON THIS PAGE</strong>
        <a href="#overview">Overview</a>
        <a href="#controller">Who we are</a>
        <a href="#access">Information and permissions</a>
        <a href="#purposes">How information is used</a>
        <a href="#storage">Storage and security</a>
        <a href="#sharing">Third parties and sharing</a>
        <a href="#retention">Retention and deletion</a>
        <a href="#rights">Your rights</a>
        <a href="#children">Children</a>
        <a href="#website">Website and cookies</a>
        <a href="#changes">Changes and contact</a>
      </aside>
      <article class="policy-article">
        <div class="draft-banner" role="note">
          <strong>Draft — do not submit to Google Play yet</strong>The developer
          name and privacy contact have been supplied; release-build SDKs, data
          transmission, advertising, and backup behavior have not been audited.
          Complete the companion <code>PRIVACY_REVIEW.md</code> checklist,
          update this document, and remove this notice and the noindex directive
          before publishing.
        </div>
        <div class="policy-summary">
          <p>
            <strong>In short:</strong> Stimmyz is designed around sound clips
            and boards stored locally on your Android device. Audio recording
            and media import begin only when you choose those features. This
            description assumes the launch app has no analytics, advertising, or
            cloud uploads; that assumption must be verified against the actual
            release build.
          </p>
        </div>
        <section aria-labelledby="overview">
          <h2 id="overview">1. Overview</h2>
          <p>
            Stimmyz (“the App”) is an Android soundboard application that lets
            you record audio, import sound clips, trim recordings, customize
            sound pads, and organize them into boards. This policy describes
            what the App may access and how that information is handled. The
            features and processing described below must reflect the version
            distributed on Google Play.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="controller">
          <h2 id="controller">2. Who is responsible for your data?</h2>
          <p>
            App: <strong>Stimmyz</strong>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Developer / data controller:{" "}
            <strong>Šarūnas Zubė, operating under the name Stimmyz</strong>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Privacy contact:{" "}
            <strong><a href="mailto:privacy@stimmyz.app">privacy@stimmyz.app</a></strong>.
          </p>
          <p>
            When you contact us, we use the information you provide (such as
            your email address and message) to respond to your inquiry. We
            retain correspondence only as needed to handle your request and
            applicable legal obligations.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="access">
          <h2 id="access">3. Information and device permissions</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>Device-audio capture:</strong> If you start this feature,
              Stimmyz requests Android's screen/audio capture authorization
              (MediaProjection) and captures audio that Android and the source
              app permit it to capture. A system permission or consent screen
              appears as applicable. Some apps prohibit capture.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Microphone:</strong> If you choose to record your own
              voice, the App requests microphone access and uses the microphone
              audio to create the clip. The App should not record microphone
              audio when you are not using a recording feature.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Imported media:</strong> If you import audio or video
              using a file picker, the App accesses the selected file to
              extract, edit, and store your sound clip.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Gallery artwork:</strong> If you add an image to a sound
              pad, the App accesses the image you select using Android's photo
              or document picker and copies it into app storage as needed.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>App settings and created content:</strong> The App stores
              your sounds, clip names, trim points, volume/repeat preferences,
              pad positions, board settings, appearance theme, and related
              information needed for the App to work.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Notifications:</strong> When needed by Android, the App
              requests notification permission to show a recording-status
              notification with a way to stop ongoing capture.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Features are user-initiated. The permissions used by the final
            release may vary by Android version.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="purposes">
          <h2 id="purposes">4. Why we use this information</h2>
          <p>
            Audio, files, images, and app preferences are used to provide the
            soundboard features you request: creating and editing clips,
            displaying artwork, remembering settings, and playing saved sounds.
            Where personal data processing is subject to the GDPR, the
            applicable legal basis is generally providing the functions you
            request, your consent where legally required (including for
            particular device access), or our legitimate interest in answering
            support inquiries. You may refuse optional permissions, but features
            requiring them will not operate.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="storage">
          <h2 id="storage">5. Local storage and security</h2>
          <p>
            Under the planned local-first design, your created sound clips,
            imported media copies, optional artwork, and board preferences are
            stored on your Android device rather than uploaded by Stimmyz to an
            app-operated cloud service. Android's app storage isolation and
            system permissions help restrict access to that content.
          </p>
          <p>
            No system can guarantee absolute security. Keep your device secure
            and avoid recording or importing material you do not have the right
            to use. If the shipped App introduces accounts, cloud sync, or
            uploads, this section must be updated before release.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="sharing">
          <h2 id="sharing">6. Third parties and data sharing</h2>
          <p>
            The planned version does not deliberately transmit your recorded
            clips, imported files, pad images, or boards to Stimmyz-operated
            servers or share them with advertisers. This must be verified by
            auditing the shipped APK/AAB and its SDKs.
          </p>
          <p>
            Android and Google Play provide system-level permissions, file
            pickers, store distribution, and related platform functionality.
            Google may process information in connection with its services
            according to its own policies. If you intentionally export or share
            a sound through an Android sharing feature, the destination is
            chosen by you.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Important:</strong> If the launch build uses advertising,
            analytics, crash reporting, remote content, or any third-party SDK
            that collects or transmits personal or device data, this policy must
            identify the data categories, uses, recipients, and any relevant
            cross-border transfers. No such SDK is assumed in this draft.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="retention">
          <h2 id="retention">7. Data retention and deletion</h2>
          <p>
            Locally saved sounds, images, and settings remain on the device
            until you delete the content, clear the App's data, or uninstall the
            App, subject to Android storage and backup behavior. Deleting a
            sound from your board or library should remove the corresponding
            data as implemented in the release version.
          </p>
          <p>
            Android device backups may preserve App data if backup is enabled in
            the release configuration and in your device settings. The developer
            must verify whether backups are enabled and describe how backed-up
            content can be deleted or excluded. Support correspondence is
            deleted when no longer needed, subject to legal requirements.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="rights">
          <h2 id="rights">8. Your choices and rights</h2>
          <p>
            You can decline recording or file permissions, stop an active
            recording, manage saved sounds and boards through the App, and clear
            the App's local data through Android settings. You may also change
            applicable permissions in Android Settings at any time.
          </p>
          <p>
            Depending on where you live, including in the European Economic
            Area, you may have rights to request access, correction, deletion,
            restriction, portability, or objection for personal data controlled
            by the developer, and to withdraw consent where processing relies on
            consent. Contact the privacy address above to make a request. Where
            data exists only on your device, the developer may be unable to
            access or retrieve it. EEA residents may lodge a complaint with
            their supervisory authority, including Lithuania's State Data
            Protection Inspectorate.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="children">
          <h2 id="children">9. Children's privacy</h2>
          <p>
            Stimmyz does not require creating an account in the planned release.
            The developer must confirm the intended age audience and applicable
            Google Play Families obligations before launch. If the App is
            marketed to children or knowingly processes children's personal
            data, additional rules and disclosures may apply.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="website">
          <h2 id="website">10. This website and cookies</h2>
          <p>
            The Stimmyz launch website is a static website and currently
            contains no advertising tags, analytics code, embedded third-party
            content, or cookies set by its own scripts. The hosting provider may
            process standard technical information, including IP addresses and
            request logs, to deliver and secure the site. Hosting-specific
            practices should be reviewed when a provider is selected.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="changes">
          <h2 id="changes">11. Policy updates and contact</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this policy as App features or data practices change.
            Changes will be posted here with an updated effective date. If a
            change requires consent or an in-app disclosure, we will provide it
            as required.
          </p>
          <p>
            For privacy questions, requests, or complaints, contact{" "}
            <a href="mailto:privacy@stimmyz.app">privacy@stimmyz.app</a>.
          </p>
        </section>
        <div class="policy-highlight">
          <p>
            <strong>Before this page goes live:</strong> Verify all permission
            and SDK disclosures, document Android backup and deletion behavior,
            then remove this drafting notice and the <code>noindex</code> meta
            tag. Set the actual effective date.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="policy-footer-note">
          This is an implementation draft, not legal advice. It must match the
          actual release build, app store disclosures, and the developer's
          circumstances.
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
